{
  "contract": "C7",
  "title": "Saved contexts: save, list and resume",
  "drafted_by": "P",
  "sources": [
    "SPEC.md §3.5 (Resume context, Pruning), §6.1, §8.1 (saved_contexts), §9.2 (Saved Groves), §10",
    "BUILD_TASKS.md §4.3 (GET_URLS, RESTORE), §4.5, P-9, S-8, S-11"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Scenario: R's shared demo set. Tab IDs come from apps/api/app/engine/fixtures/demo_tabs.json (the 28 tabs in snapshot.example.json); project, claim, note and saved-context IDs come from grove.example.json and memory-search.example.json. IDs these examples create are listed in `introduces`; IDs that belong to another user are listed in `unknown_ids`.",
    "Every request carries Authorization: Bearer <token> unless the example lists request.headers explicitly. user_id never appears in a request body; the server takes it from the token.",
    "Durations are integer milliseconds (active_ms) so every sum is exact; the UI converts to minutes. Times are UTC and follow R's story clock (snapshot at 2026-10-04T11:40:00Z).",
    "Errors are RFC 7807 problem JSON with `instance` = the request path, as in R's files.",
    "Save: POST /api/projects/{project_id}/save-context. kind is 'resume' (card required) or 'references' (card null; the prune dialog's save_as_references action, before the tabs are closed).",
    "The grove page builds the card from the grove it shows: goal, direction, decisions (stones), unresolved_questions (open mushrooms) and next_action are R's claim objects copied unchanged from grove.example.json; explored_branches lists branches with status 'explored'. The server stores card and tabs as sent and never re-derives a claim.",
    "tabs[].fallback_url is the stripped URL from the bridge's GET_URLS (no query string, no fragment; one with ? or # returns 422). These are the only URLs that reach the server (SPEC §6.1) and become RESTORE fallback_urls after a browser restart.",
    "tabs[].important follows the tree's important_tab_refs. tabs[].excluded_reason is exact_duplicate, semantic_redundant or stale (R's prune kinds) or null; such tabs are never important and are left out of the default restore.",
    "Resume: POST /api/contexts/{context_id}/resume (no body) sets last_resumed_at and returns the card plus live totals across all of the project's sessions: 8,040,000 ms = 134 min, R's attention_min, across 3 sessions (Oct 2, and the two in sessions.example.json).",
    "important_tabs are ordered by live cluster_tabs.importance (R's leaf importance); if the cluster is gone, importance is null and the saved order is kept. totals_as_of is null when totals are live; for contexts whose events aged out of retention it is the save time, and the totals are those recorded then (the March 12 context).",
    "List rows carry counts for the Saved Groves cards; time formatting such as '2 h 14 m' is left to the UI.",
    "A project or context the caller does not own returns 404."
  ],
